<title>MEXICO: Mexico says Canada approves its pork, beef.</title>
<headline>Mexico says Canada approves its pork, beef.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada has approved Mexico's inspection program for pork and beef, which should open up that market for Mexican exports, the Mexican Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Development said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Mexican ministry said that the Canadian government had found the state of Sonora to be free of swine fever.</p>
<p>It said the entire country has been certified to be free of cattle diseases.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559))</p>
</text>
